 "comment": "CATALOG-BAKE-1 (apex-071): HAND-CURATED per-model wire semantics \u2014 the single place O/H-class per-model values live (comb doc config-row-comb-20260918.md section 3 field classes). v2 (operator-adjudicated 3-delta, 2026-09-19): the merged generated+overlay catalog bakes IN PLACE into default_models.json (upstream shape: role pins + models array), so this file also carries the role pins (default/web_search/image_description/session_summary) and the `bake` list \u2014 overlay-only models that must ride the merged catalog (seed migration; grok-4.5 is not on the proxy). The gate (scripts/catalog_gate.py) is FAIL-CLOSED: REQUIRED_FIELDS = api_backend + model_family must be present on every entry, and every generated model needs a complete entry \u2014 a missing curation is a build failure, never a silent bless. Seed migration: the pre-bake seed rows (grok-4.6, grok-4.5, gpt-5.6-sol) migrate byte-for-value into their entries; config-derived fields win on collision (grok-4.6 supports_backend_search=false; sol 5-item O-class menu beat the old 6-item seed menu). New-model api_backend rulings follow the codebase slug-inference convention (xai-grok-sampling-types/src/catalog_wire.rs) so the curation equals the effective wire: o-series + gpt-5+ + gpt-4.1/gpt-4o => responses; gpt-4.x chat / gpt-3.5 / embeddings => chat_completions. C-class (operator ruling, CATALOG-CCLASS-SEED-1 / apex-byc, 2026-09-19): context_window + max_completion_tokens are C-class \u2014 the generated catalog is the proxy's truth for the baked caps, config.toml rows remain the top runtime override, and overlay entries for models that ARE in the generated catalog (on the proxy) must not carry them (the gate fails closed on FORBIDDEN_OVERLAY_FIELDS; the merge never lets an overlay cap beat a generated cap). Overlay-only models (not on the proxy \u2014 grok-4.5 bake-listed, gemma-4-31b between-build) may carry them: the overlay is the sole source of caps for those rows. Excluded by design: base_url + env_key ([endpoints] defaults cover them). gemma-4-31b is overlay-only by design (between-build config row; it bakes once listed in `bake`). Precedence UNCHANGED: config row > live fetch > baked catalog > fallback. Anthropic rows are pinned to messages explicitly \u2014 never left to inference. v3 (ZC-SUBSET-CURATION-1 / apex-ayl.129, operator-approved 8-row zero-config menu, 2026-09-22): `models` is shrunk to the curated 8-row menu (gpt-5.6-sol/terra/luna, claude-opus-5/sonnet-5, grok-4.6, gemini-3.8-flash, gemini-3.1-pro-preview \u2014 values byte-exact, operator value review pending); `bake` is empty (grok-4.5 removed from the menu); `skip` lists every on-proxy model outside the 8 core with a per-class reason (the .128 subset-drift contract: curated \u222a skipped \u222a alerted covers the whole proxy). v4 (operator ruling 2026-09-22, mid-apex-ayl.129): all four role pins move grok-4.6 -> gpt-5.6-terra \u2014 grok-vertex has major issues and the title-gen (session_summary) path is actively 500ing on the Vertex grok-4.6 deployment (litellm pydantic tool_choice error, every run); every harness-internal role pin leaves the broken Vertex deployment. The grok-4.6 ROW stays in the 8-row catalog for explicit /model use. v5 (ZC-EAST2-UNPIN-1 / apex-ayl.126.6, 2026-09-23): the x-litellm-tags \"East US 2\" pin is REMOVED from the 3 gpt-5.6 rows (sol/terra/luna). Original justifications superseded — (a) the glm tagged-401 era is fixed proxy-side, and (b) TAGPROBE-3 (live, 2026-09-23) replayed encrypted_content reasoning verbatim across 3 untagged gpt-5.6-terra turns: all 200, reasoning 8-11 tokens per turn (persisted 2026-09-23 re-run: 8/9/11 at /tmp/tagprobe3-rerun-20260923.txt; per-run LLM variance), cross-turn context recalled (litellm_enc blobs are model-keyed, not deployment-keyed). Residual risk (accepted, documented): if the untagged view later goes multi-deployment with distinct key material, enc-affinity degrades Retain→RetainOptimistic; the reactive strip-fallback recovers (XW-ENC-AFFINITY-1 design §3.3). The operator unpin toggle (empty x-litellm-tags row header) now truly reaches the wire — UNPIN-TOGGLE-WIRE-1 (apex-ayl.126.5). v6 (CTXWIN-BAKED-ONLY-1 / apex-1k7, operator ruling 2026-09-24): the paired curated rows now carry the FLEET RUNTIME context_window — in the no-endpoint (Linux apex-release) tier the baked catalog IS the config tier, so the paired bases ride the live config-tier standard (sol/opus 262144, terra/sonnet 500000) and the four -1m twins ride 1048576 (the 1M-variant pair is only meaningful if the two windows differ); the gate is amended: the curated overlay context_window beats the generated cap, max_completion_tokens stays generated-truth (forbidden in the overlay).",
